15:["$","p","b535",{"children":["The financial burden of AI is often underestimated because it creeps in $20 at a time. But the true cost isn't just the dollar amount, it's the friction. Consider a typical video production workflow:"]}]
16:["$","div","b536",{"role":"region","aria-label":"Comparison table, scroll horizontally to see all columns","tabIndex":0,"data-lenis-prevent":true,"className":"my-10 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-orange","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left","children":["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","b537",{"className":"bg-black/[0.04]","children":[["$","td","b5370",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b540",{"children":[["$","strong","b539",{"children":["Stage"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b5371",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b543",{"children":[["$","strong","b542",{"children":["Typical tool"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b5372",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b546",{"children":[["$","strong","b545",{"children":["Monthly cost"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b547",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b5470",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b550",{"children":["Scripting"]}]]}],["$","td","b5471",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b553",{"children":["ChatGPT"]}]]}],["$","td","b5472",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b556",{"children":["$$20"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b557",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b5570",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b560",{"children":["Voiceover"]}]]}],["$","td","b5571",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b563",{"children":["ElevenLabs (Creator tier)"]}]]}],["$","td","b5572",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b566",{"children":["$$22"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b567",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b5670",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b570",{"children":["Visuals"]}]]}],["$","td","b5671",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b573",{"children":["Midjourney or Flux"]}]]}],["$","td","b5672",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b576",{"children":["$$10â€“$30"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b577",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b5770",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b580",{"children":["Animation"]}]]}],["$","td","b5771",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b583",{"children":["Kling AI or Luma Dream Machine"]}]]}],["$","td","b5772",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b586",{"children":["$$30"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b587",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b5870",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b590",{"children":[["$","strong","b589",{"children":["Total"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b5871",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b593",{"children":[["$","strong","b592",{"children":["Four interfaces, four silos"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b5872",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b596",{"children":[["$","strong","b595",{"children":["$$82â€“$102"]}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}]}]
17:["$","p","b598",{"children":["This fragmented stack forces you to navigate four different interfaces, four different credit systems, and four different usage caps. If you hit a limit on Kling, you can't borrow credits from your unused ElevenLabs quota. You're locked into silos. This inefficiency is the primary driver behind the rise of AI aggregators, platforms that consolidate these specialized engines into a single, cohesive workflow."]}]
18:["$","h2","b600",{"id":"defining-the-all-in-one-creative-standard","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Defining the all-in-one creative standard"]}]
19:["$","p","b604",{"children":["Not every platform that claims to be all-in-one actually delivers. Many are simply LLM wrappers, interfaces that connect to a chat model and maybe one basic image generator. To be a true creative powerhouse, a platform must master the ",["$","strong","b602",{"children":["Triple Threat"]}]," of modalities:"]}]
1a:["$","ul","b607-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b607",{"children":[["$","strong","b605",{"children":["Image generation. "]}],"A spread of state-of-the-art models like GPT Image 2, Nano Banana Pro, and Seedream, which handle text-in-image, style control, and anatomical accuracy far better than older models. No single one wins every brief, so you want the choice."]}],["$","li","b610",{"children":[["$","strong","b608",{"children":["Video generation. "]}],"Access to frontier models like Kling and Seedance, capable of consistent physics and high-resolution motion."]}],["$","li","b613",{"children":[["$","strong","b611",{"children":["Audio generation. "]}],"High-fidelity voice synthesis and music from ElevenLabs, plus reference-driven voices from ByteDance's Seed Audio."]}]]}]
1b:["$","p","b615",{"children":["When evaluating a unified platform, use this checklist to make sure you aren't sacrificing quality for convenience:"]}]
1c:["$","ol","b618-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b618",{"children":[["$","strong","b616",{"children":["API parity. "]}],"Does the platform offer the same settings (guidance scale, seed control, aspect ratios) as the native tools?"]}],["$","li","b621",{"children":[["$","strong","b619",{"children":["Model latency. "]}],"Is there a significant delay between clicking generate and the model responding?"]}],["$","li","b624",{"children":[["$","strong","b622",{"children":["Modal diversity. "]}],"Does it cover the full Triple Threat, or is it heavily weighted toward just text?"]}]]}]
1d:["$","h2","b626",{"id":"melius-consolidating-your-creative-workflow","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Melius: consolidating your creative workflow"]}]
1e:["$","p","b640",{"children":["Melius is built specifically to bridge the gap between high-end generative power and cost-efficiency. By integrating frontier models like ",["$","strong","b628",{"children":["Kling"]}]," and ",["$","strong","b630",{"children":["Seedance"]}]," for video, ",["$","strong","b632",{"children":["GPT Image 2"]}]," and ",["$","strong","b634",{"children":["Nano Banana Pro"]}]," for imagery, and ",["$","strong","b636",{"children":["ElevenLabs"]}]," and ",["$","strong","b638",{"children":["Seed Audio"]}]," for audio under one billing umbrella, it eliminates the need for a dozen separate logins."]}]
1f:["$","p","b642",{"children":[["$","strong","b641",{"children":["Can a single subscription truly replace specialized AI tools without losing quality?"]}]]}]
20:["$","p","b644",{"children":["Yes, provided the platform maintains direct API parity with flagship models like Kling and ElevenLabs. Melius achieves this by acting as a unified creative canvas where you can generate a cinematic shot in Kling, overlay a voiceover from ElevenLabs, and refine the prompt with a frontier text model, all within the same interface. This consolidation doesn't just lower monthly costs by up to 60%, it removes the cognitive load of switching contexts, letting you focus on the narrative rather than the tech stack."]}]
21:["$","p","b648",{"children":["The advantage here isn't just the unified billing, it's the ",["$","strong","b646",{"children":["unified interface"]}],". In a fragmented stack, your assets are scattered across four different gallery pages. In Melius, your video, audio, and images live in a single project ecosystem, making it significantly easier to iterate on a concept without losing your momentum."]}]
22:["$","h2","b650",{"id":"why-the-canvas-and-the-agent-are-the-real-unlock","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Why the canvas and the agent are the real unlock"]}]
23:["$","p","b656",{"children":["Access to every model is table stakes. A dropdown of frontier engines is only as good as your ability to point the right one at the right job and prompt it well, and that is exactly where a bare LLM wrapper falls down. Melius is built on two things a flat list of models doesn't have: a ",["$","strong","b652",{"children":["node-based creative canvas"]}]," and an ",["$","strong","b654",{"children":["agentic harness"]}],"."]}]
24:["$","p","b666",{"children":["On the canvas, every prompt, image, video clip, and audio track is a node, and the edges between them carry data from one step to the next. An image node feeds a video node, a script node feeds a voiceover, a still becomes the key frame for a shot. The structure of your project is visible and connected, not buried in a dozen separate chat histories. That shared graph is what gives the platform ",["$","strong","b658",{"children":["context across models"]}],": the output of a ",["$","$L3e","b661",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b660","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false},"children":["Nano Banana Pro"]}]," image can flow directly into a Kling or ",["$","$L3e","b664",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b663","href":"/blog/seedance-2-5-anticipation","isNewTab":false},"children":["Seedance"]}]," video, and the same brief and brand context inform every generation on the board."]}]
25:["$","p","b670",{"children":["Sitting on top of that canvas is Mel, the built-in creative-director agent. Because Mel can see the whole graph, it does the part most people get wrong on their own: it ",["$","strong","b668",{"children":["orchestrates"]}]," the work. It decides which model fits each step, wires the nodes together in the right order, and translates your intent into the specific prompt each model actually responds to. Kling wants motion described a certain way; an image model wants composition and lens; ElevenLabs wants direction on tone and pacing. Mel handles that per-model prompt craft so you don't have to learn the quirks of ten different tools."]}]
26:["$","p","b677",{"children":["This is why the platform gets more ",["$","em","b672",{"children":["right"]}]," than a raw list of APIs ever could. The models are the engines, but the canvas gives them shared context and the agent knows how to drive them. A single creative director can hand Mel a brief and get back a coherent, multi-model workflow, generated, connected, and on-brand, the ",["$","$L3e","b675",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b674","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false},"children":["brief-to-execution workflow"]}]," in one place, instead of manually copying assets between four tabs and re-explaining the concept to each one."]}]
27:["$","h2","b679",{"id":"performance-vs-price-why-aggregators-are-winning","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Performance vs. price: why aggregators are winning"]}]
28:["$","p","b681",{"children":["The legacy model of AI subscriptions asks you to bet on a single horse. If you subscribe to one specific video generator, you're stuck with their version of reality for the month. If a better model drops two weeks later, you're either stuck or paying for a second subscription."]}]
29:["$","p","b685",{"children":["The aggregator model offers ",["$","strong","b683",{"children":["model agnosticism"]}],". This is the ultimate future-proofing for a creator. When a new version of Flux or a new competitor to Kling is released, an aggregator like Melius can integrate it into the existing dashboard. You don't have to change your workflow or update your billing, you just select the new model from a dropdown."]}]
2a:["$","p","b687",{"children":["This flexibility allows for a best-of-breed approach. You might find that for a specific project, one model handles lighting better while another handles character consistency. On an aggregator platform, you can test both for the price of one, rather than being locked into the limitations of a single provider."]}]
2b:["$","h2","b689",{"id":"how-to-migrate-your-creative-projects-to-a-unified-platform","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["How to migrate your creative projects to a unified platform"]}]
2c:["$","p","b691",{"children":["Transitioning from a fragmented stack to a unified platform like Melius doesn't have to happen overnight. Here is a practical three-step plan to reclaim your workflow."]}]
2d:["$","ol","b694-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b694",{"children":[["$","strong","b692",{"children":["The subscription audit. "]}],"List every AI tool you currently pay for. Identify the usage gap, models you pay $20 a month for but only use three or four times. These are the first candidates for consolidation."]}],["$","li","b697",{"children":[["$","strong","b695",{"children":["The output benchmark. "]}],"Before canceling your standalone subscriptions, run your most common prompts through Melius. Compare the Kling video output or the ElevenLabs voice clarity against the native apps. With proper API integration, you'll find the results are identical."]}],["$","li","b700",{"children":[["$","strong","b698",{"children":["Centralize your assets. "]}],"Start a new project within Melius and generate all assets (image, video, and audio) for that specific campaign in the unified canvas. Once you experience the lack of tab-switching, the friction of the old fragmented way becomes much more apparent."]}]]}]
2e:["$","p","b705",{"children":["The era of paying for five different $20 subscriptions is ending. By moving to a unified platform, you aren't just saving money, you're buying back the time and mental energy required to actually be a creator. ",["$","$L3e","b703",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b702","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["Start creating with Melius"]}],"."]}]
2f:["$","h2","b707",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
30:["$","div","b708",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can a single subscription truly replace specialized AI tools without losing quality?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes, provided the platform maintains direct API parity with flagship models like Kling and ElevenLabs. Melius achieves this by acting as a unified creative canvas where you can generate a cinematic shot in Kling, overlay a voiceover from ElevenLabs, and refine the prompt with a frontier text model, all within the same interface. This consolidation doesn't just lower monthly costs; it removes the cognitive load of switching contexts, so you focus on the narrative rather than the tech stack."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is subscription bloat, or the AI tax?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Subscription bloat is what happens when a creative stack is assembled one $20 tool at a time. Text generation, voiceover, image generation, and video generation each arrive as a separate subscription, and a typical stack easily clears $100 a month. The hidden cost isn't only the dollar amount, it's the friction of four interfaces, four credit systems, and four usage caps that can't share quota."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is an AI aggregator?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"An AI aggregator is a platform that consolidates specialized generative engines, for image, video, and audio, into a single workflow and one billing umbrella. Instead of subscribing to each provider directly, you access frontier models like Kling and Seedance for video, GPT Image 2 and Nano Banana Pro for images, and ElevenLabs and Seed Audio for audio through one interface, with one credit pool and one place your assets live. The best aggregators go further, adding a shared context and an agent that orchestrates those models for you rather than just listing them."}]]}],"$L3f","$L40","$L41","$L42"]}]
31:["$","p","b713",{"children":["For a film-specific comparison of shot control, continuity and editing, read ",["$","$L3e","b711",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b710","href":"/blog/ai-video-generators-filmmakers-compared","isNewTab":false},"children":["AI video generators for filmmakers, compared"]}],"."]}]
32:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L43","post-static-ad-from-style-reference",{"post":{"_key":"post-static-ad-from-style-reference","slug":"static-ad-from-style-reference","category":"guides","title":"How to build a static ad from a style reference on Melius","isoDate":"2026-09-11","date":"September 11, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Point an agent at a moodboard and ask for statics in that style. The brief that does it, what the agent builds in the background, and where you steer.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/static-ad-from-style-reference/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"Do I have to use the canvas to make static ads on Melius?","answer":"No. You can brief the agent and steer the results, and plenty of people work that way. The canvas is where the agent's work becomes visible and editable, so you'll open it to fix the outputs that missed, but you don't wire the workflow yourself unless you want to."},{"question":"What should I put in the brief?","answer":"The goal, your references, and the constraints that matter: how many variations, which ratios you ship, and the brand anchor to check against. Our example for this workflow is a single sentence asking it to use the Image Style Analysis template with your reference images and return a style description for new variants. Brief the whole job at once rather than one step at a time."},{"question":"Will the agent generate before checking with me?","answer":"That depends on the mode. In ask-permission mode it raises clarifying questions before each major step, which suits high-stakes work where you want to see every decision. In auto-run it decides and builds while you're elsewhere, so a brief sent between meetings has a canvas of results waiting when you get back."},{"question":"How many reference images should I give it?","answer":"Two to four is usually enough, and the recipe works to a range of two to ten. That ceiling is editorial, not technical: individual models accept many more. More references do not produce a more accurate style description, because the analysis describes what your references have in common, so a sixth image sharing less with the others widens the description instead of sharpening it."},{"question":"Can I use a competitor's ad as a style reference?","answer":"Yes, and it's one of the most common inputs for this workflow, alongside your own past campaigns and fashion editorials. The analysis returns a description of photographic qualities such as light, palette and composition rather than a copy of the image, and you're generating your own subject against that description."},{"question":"Can I reuse a style that worked?","answer":"Yes. The style description is a text node, so it copies and pastes between canvases and you can point a later brief at it. Once one reliably produces on-brand output it becomes a small reusable asset you start every campaign canvas from."},{"question":"How much does a batch of static ads cost to run?","answer":"Generating on Melius runs on credits, drawn from the same pool whichever model a step uses, so comparing two models on the same shot costs no more to set up than running one. Current plans and credit allowances are on the pricing page."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"key-takeaways","title":"Key takeaways"},{"_key":"static-ads-that-match-a-look-you-already-have","title":"Match a look"},{"_key":"what-you-actually-type","title":"What you type"},{"_key":"what-the-agent-does-in-the-background","title":"In the background"},{"_key":"where-you-step-in","title":"Where you step in"},{"_key":"where-this-workflow-goes-wrong","title":"Where it goes wrong"},{"_key":"why-the-canvas-is-still-there","title":"Why the canvas"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5089","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5088","text":"Key takeaways","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"key-takeaways"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5092","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5090","text":"You brief an agent; you don't wire the workflow. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5091","text":"One instruction naming your references and the output you want is enough. The agent picks the models, writes the prompts, creates the nodes and connects them up.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5095","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5093","text":"The steps still happen, and you can watch them happen. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5094","text":"Reference grouping, style analysis, model choice, variation count: the agent does each one as a visible node rather than behind a loading spinner.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5098","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5096","text":"Expect to finish the last mile yourself. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5097","text":"We put the agent's first pass at 85% to 95% of the way there. The rest is prompt tweaks on individual nodes, and that's where your judgement goes.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5101","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5099","text":"Brief the whole job, not the next step. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5100","text":"Asking for the references, the variations, every ratio and a brand check in one instruction costs the same as asking for one of them.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5104","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5102","text":"Ambiguity gets a question, not a guess. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5103","text":"In ask-permission mode the agent checks aspect ratio, audience and tone before it spends a generation. In auto-run it decides and builds while you're elsewhere.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5106","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5105","text":"Static ads that match a look you already have","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"static-ads-that-match-a-look-you-already-have"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5108","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5107","text":"To build a static ad from a style reference on Melius, you brief the Mel agent: point it at your reference images and ask for new statics in that style. It assembles the canvas, runs the style analysis, chooses the models, generates the variations, and leaves every step visible so you can correct the ones that missed. From brief to assets you can download runs about 10 to 15 minutes.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5110","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5109","text":"Most of the work in matching a look goes into describing it. You know the campaign you want to sit next to, and you can see exactly why it works, but turning that into instructions a model will follow is the step that eats an afternoon. That's the step you're handing over.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5112","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5111","text":"What you actually type","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-you-actually-type"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5114","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5113","text":"Right-click anywhere on the canvas and choose Ask Mel, or press the forward slash key. Anything you have selected goes in as a reference automatically. Then describe the job. You don't need to name the model, set the resolution, or say which output connects to which input. Mel will do these for you.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5119","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5116","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5115","text":"Our standing advice is to ask for more than you think will work. A brief naming the references, the number of variations, every ratio you ship and a brand check against your brand anchor costs no more to write than one asking for a single image, and if the agent can't cover the whole job it tells you. Brief it the way you'd brief a designer, with a concrete goal and real constraints, not the way you'd chat. This is the same ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5117","text":"brief-to-execution workflow","marks":["b5116"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5118","text":" applied to a single look.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5121","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5120","text":"What the agent does in the background","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-the-agent-does-in-the-background"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5123","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5122","text":"None of this needs doing by hand, and all of it stays inspectable while it happens. A cyan marker on the canvas shows where the agent is currently building.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5126","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5124","text":"Reads your brand anchor. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5125","text":"If you keep one, the node holding your voice, palette and type gets pulled in as context before anything generates.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5129","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5127","text":"Groups the references. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5128","text":"Your reference images become a single unified group, so the analysis reaches all of them on one edge instead of one per image.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5132","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5130","text":"Runs the style analysis. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5131","text":"The Image Style Analysis template comes preconfigured but has inputs that need wiring, which is exactly the case to hand to the agent. It returns a written description: palette, direction and quality of the light, mood, composition, depth of field, shot type.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5138","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5135","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5133","text":"Picks the model per step. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5134","text":"Melius recommends ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5136","text":"Nano Banana Pro","marks":["b5135"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5137","text":" for hewing to a photographic look, and GPT Image 2 where the ad carries visible copy, its High tier for production output. You can override that on any node.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5141","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5139","text":"Writes the prompt. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5140","text":"Because the style description carries the look, the generation prompt only has to name the subject and where it sits. Short prompts win here, and the agent knows it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5144","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5142","text":"Builds the image nodes and connects them. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5143","text":"Style description into the image node, resolution set, ratio set per placement. The node hides any ratio the chosen model can't produce.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5147","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5145","text":"Runs the variations in parallel. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5146","text":"Image models are probabilistic, so several takes at once beats one take and a retry. Ask for every ratio in the same brief and it queues those together too.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5149","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5148","text":"Where you step in","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"where-you-step-in"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5151","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5150","text":"The first pass gets you most of the way, not all of it. We put that at 85% to 95%, and the last stretch is the part worth your attention, because it's taste rather than assembly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5154","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5152","text":"Work at the node, not in the chat. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5153","text":"Open the one image that nearly landed, edit its prompt with the specific correction, and re-run that node alone. Product too small in frame becomes a line saying the product fills 40% of the frame width. Colour drifting green becomes a warmer grade with terracotta in the highlights. Illegible type on a label means switching that node to GPT Image 2 High.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5156","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5155","text":"Go back to the agent for the genuinely bulk things: swapping a model across multiple nodes, regenerating everything with the brand anchor attached, resizing ten nodes into three ratios each.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5158","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5157","text":"One habit worth forming. The agent doesn't automatically know about an edit you made by hand, so if you later ask it to repeat that treatment across the canvas it may revert to its original approach. Either make the change on a shared context node like the brand anchor, where it propagates on the next run, or tell the agent what you changed and ask it to apply that too.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5160","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5159","text":"Where this workflow goes wrong","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"where-this-workflow-goes-wrong"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5163","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5161","text":"The brief was too small. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5162","text":"Describing one step, running it, then describing the next is the safe instinct and it costs you the afternoon. A re-brief is cheap; orchestrating by hand is not.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5166","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5164","text":"The references disagree with each other. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5165","text":"Five fashion editorials and one storefront screenshot do not share a look, and the description will average them into something you didn't ask for. The agent can only describe what your set has in common.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5169","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5167","text":"The agent got treated like a chatbot. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5168","text":"It isn't a chat window, it builds canvases. Conversational back-and-forth gets far less out of it than one concrete brief carrying references and constraints.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5172","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5170","text":"One node got edited fifteen times. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5171","text":"Past about the fifth tweak the problem usually isn't the prompt. Step back and re-brief, because the agent has the whole canvas as context and will often unstick it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5175","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5173","text":"The output was judged on the canvas preview. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5174","text":"Previews are downscaled at every resolution to keep the canvas quick. Open a variation full screen, or download it, before you rule it out.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5177","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5176","text":"Why the canvas is still there","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-the-canvas-is-still-there"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5179","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5178","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work, and underneath the agent is a node-based canvas where every model call is a node and edges pass one node's output into the next. The canvas isn't something you have to learn before you can work. It's there so the agent's decisions are legible: which model ran, what prompt it wrote, which reference fed which step.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5181","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5180","text":"That's what separates this from describing what you want in a chat and hoping. Nothing here is a black box. When an output is wrong you find the node where it went wrong, change that one thing, and re-run everything downstream of it. Earlier node canvases were built before agents existed and assumed a human would wire up every node; this one exists so you can see and steer the work instead of performing it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5186","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5183","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5182","text":"The models sit behind ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5184","text":"one subscription","marks":["b5183"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5185","text":". Melius spans a library of leading models for image, video and audio, and the agent routes each step to the right one unless you choose per node.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5188","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5187","text":"You own the content you create on Melius and can use, publish, and distribute it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms. Melius doesn't claim ownership of your work and doesn't use it to train AI models.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5193","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5190","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5189","text":"Have a look you want to hit? ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5191","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b5190"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5192","text":", drop your references on a canvas, and tell the agent what you want.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5198","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5195","href":"/blog/text-to-speech-voiceover","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5194","text":"For the next step, see ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5196","text":"turning a script into a natural voiceover","marks":["b5195"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5197","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5200","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5199","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b5201","items":"$32:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5206","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5203","href":"/blog/product-hero-shot","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5202","text":"For product photography, follow our ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5204","text":"product hero shot workflow","marks":["b5203"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5205","text":" to keep specifications, branding, and style references separate.","marks":[]}]}]}}],"$L44","$L45"]}]]}]]}]
35:null
3d:"$d:props:children:1:props:serverProvidedParams:params"
7:300
3f:["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the best AI aggregator?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"The best AI aggregator is the one that does more than list models behind one login. Look for three things: real API parity with the flagship models (so quality isn't sacrificed for convenience), one shared credit pool so you aren't rationing across silos, and an orchestration layer, a canvas plus an agent, that wires the models together and prompts each one correctly. Melius is built around exactly that: every major model on a node-based canvas, one credit pool, and Mel, an agent that plans and routes the work."}]]}]
40:["$","details","4",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Why does an aggregator get better results than using the models directly?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Because access to the models is only half the problem, the other half is orchestration. Melius is built on a node-based creative canvas where every prompt, image, video, and audio track is a connected node, so the output of one model can flow into the next and every generation shares the same brief and brand context. On top of that sits Mel, an agent that can see the whole graph, choose the right model for each step, wire the workflow together, and write the specific prompt each model responds to. A flat list of APIs can't do that, which is why context across models and agentic orchestration are what actually make the results land."}]]}]
41:["$","details","5",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is model agnosticism, and why does it matter?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Model agnosticism means your workflow isn't locked to a single provider. When a new version of a model drops, an aggregator can add it to the existing dashboard, so you select it from a dropdown instead of buying another subscription or rebuilding your process. It lets you take a best-of-breed approach, testing one model for lighting and another for character consistency, for the price of one."}]]}]
42:["$","details","6",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["How much can I save by consolidating AI subscriptions?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"A fragmented stack of scripting, voiceover, imagery, and animation tools typically runs $82 to $102 per month. Moving that work onto a single aggregator can lower monthly costs by up to 60%, and it recovers the time otherwise lost to managing billing cycles and switching tabs."}]]}]
44:["$","$L43","post-brief-to-execution-workflow",{"post":{"_key":"post-brief-to-execution-workflow","slug":"brief-to-execution-workflow","category":"modus-news","title":"The Brief-to-Execution workflow for creative teams","isoDate":"2026-07-16","date":"July 16, 2026","readTime":"7 Min Read","excerpt":"One-shot prompting has a ceiling. The agencies that win aren't the ones with the best prompt. They're the ones that turn a single master brief into a full, on-brand campaign. Here is the Brief-to-Execution workflow, and how an orchestration layer like Melius splits the Labor of Execution from the Labor of Taste.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/brief-to-execution/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the Brief-to-Execution workflow?","answer":"Brief-to-Execution is a structured way of running creative production where a single master brief becomes the source of truth for every asset. Instead of prompting AI models one by one, a human defines the strategy, an orchestration layer like Melius turns that intent into work on a shared canvas, routing each job to the right model and holding every output to one brand context, and the human returns to select and polish the best results. It moves the work from fragmented chats into one unified production line."},{"question":"How does the Brief-to-Execution framework solve inconsistency in AI creative work?","answer":"By establishing a singular master brief as the source of truth, the framework ensures every output, whether copy, imagery, or video, derives from the same strategic intent rather than isolated prompts. This eliminates the drift that occurs when designers and writers prompt models independently, so a social post and a video script stay on-brand because they draw on the same brief and the same brand context."},{"question":"What is the difference between the Labor of Execution and the Labor of Taste?","answer":"The Labor of Execution is the repetitive, high-volume work: generating copy variations, resizing a master visual for fifteen aspect ratios, keeping every asset against your brand context. Agents handle it. The Labor of Taste is judgment: setting the creative vision, defining the never-go zones, and picking the one concept with the spark. Humans keep it."},{"question":"What does an orchestration layer like Melius actually do?","answer":"You store your brand context with Melius once, written instructions plus reference images, and Mel, its creative-director agent, applies it to every prompt, node title, and output automatically. Mel plans the work on a shared canvas and routes each job to the best model for it, so you steer in plain language instead of rewriting prompts one at a time."},{"question":"Why isn't one-shot prompting enough for agencies?","answer":"One-shot prompting forces a human to act as a manual operator, micromanaging each output in isolation. It doesn't scale, and it produces drift because every prompt is disconnected from the last. Agencies that need volume without losing brand consistency have to move from operating tools to architecting systems."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"why-individual-models-aren-t-enough","title":"The prompting ceiling"},{"_key":"defining-the-brief-to-execution-framework","title":"The framework"},{"_key":"the-human-as-creative-director","title":"The creative director"},{"_key":"orchestrating-with-melius","title":"Orchestration"},{"_key":"future-proofing-the-agency-workflow","title":"Future-proofing"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b407","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b404","text":"The competitive advantage in creative work is shifting. It is moving away from the person who can coax the best single output from a model, and toward the team that can turn a strategy into a full campaign without losing its brand soul along the way. That shift has a shape, and it is worth naming: the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b405","text":"Brief-to-Execution","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b406","text":" workflow.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b409","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b408","text":"Why individual models aren't enough","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-individual-models-aren-t-enough"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b411","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b410","text":"The early days of generative AI were defined by the prompt. Creative professionals spent hours refining the perfect string of words to get a single image or a halfway-decent paragraph of copy. That era, the era of the prompt engineer, is hitting a ceiling. In a professional agency setting, one-shot prompting is an inefficient bottleneck. It requires the human to act as a manual operator, micromanaging every single output in isolation.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b417","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b412","text":"The real challenge for agencies today isn't ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b413","text":"how do I talk to a chatbot?","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b414","text":" but ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b415","text":"how do I scale creative production without losing brand soul?","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b416","text":" When you are prompting models one by one, you aren't being creative. You're being a data-entry clerk for an LLM. To move past this, we have to transition from being tool-operators to becoming system-architects.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b419","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b418","text":"The system-architect paradigm","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b424","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b420","text":"The system-architect paradigm is the transition from manually manipulating individual model inputs to designing automated, interconnected workflows that carry a high-level goal from brief to finished assets. Instead of asking ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b421","text":"what is the best prompt for this headline?","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b422","text":", the system-architect asks ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b423","text":"how do I build a pipeline that takes a 10-page brand strategy and turns it into 50 unique, on-brand assets?","marks":["em"]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b426","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b425","text":"Defining the Brief-to-Execution framework","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"defining-the-brief-to-execution-framework"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b428","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b427","text":"The solution to prompting fatigue is a structured Brief-to-Execution framework. This methodology moves the generative AI workflow away from fragmented chats and into a unified production line, where agents handle the volume and humans handle the vision.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b430","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b429","text":"By establishing a singular master brief as the source of truth, the framework ensures that every output, whether copy, visual assets, or video, derives from the same strategic intent rather than isolated, manual prompts. This shifts the human role from manual execution to orchestration, allowing for a cohesive multi-channel campaign where every output, from a social post to a video script, maintains brand alignment because it draws on the same brief and the same brand context. This centralized approach eliminates the drift that occurs when individual designers or writers prompt AI models independently, keeping the final execution close to the original strategy.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b432","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b431","text":"The framework consists of three distinct phases.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b435","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b433","text":"Strategic intent (human). ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b434","text":"The human defines the why and the who. This is the master brief containing brand voice, audience personas, and campaign goals.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b438","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b436","text":"Agent orchestration (Melius). ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b437","text":"The brief is ingested into an orchestration layer like Melius, which breaks the high-level intent into actionable tasks and builds them out on a shared canvas.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b441","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b439","text":"Refined output (human). ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b440","text":"The agents produce the Labor of Execution, and the human returns to perform the final Labor of Taste, selecting and polishing the best versions.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b443","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b442","text":"The human as creative director","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-human-as-creative-director"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b449","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b444","text":"In this new workflow, the human role evolves into that of a creative director. A creative director doesn't necessarily pick up the brush; they set the constraints and judge the results. This shift is critical because it separates the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b445","text":"Labor of Execution","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b446","text":" from the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b447","text":"Labor of Taste","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b448","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b451","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b450","text":"The Labor of Execution, assigned to agents","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b453","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b452","text":"Agents are far superior to humans at the repetitive, high-volume tasks that traditionally eat up agency hours.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b456","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b454","text":"Variations. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b455","text":"Creating 20 different versions of a headline for A/B testing.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b459","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b457","text":"Formatting. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b458","text":"Resizing a master visual for 15 different social-media aspect ratios.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b465","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b462","href":"/blog/static-ad-from-style-reference","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b460","text":"Contextualization. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b461","text":"Taking one campaign concept and building out the full set (the social cut, the email header, the video storyboard) all drawn from the same brief, or ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b463","text":"building a static ad from a style reference","marks":["b462"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b464","text":" so a new subject matches a look you already have.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b468","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b466","text":"On-brand output. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b467","text":"Holding every asset to the same stored brand context (voice, palette, typography, reference imagery) instead of eyeballing a 50-page guidelines deck by hand.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b470","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b469","text":"The Labor of Taste, retained by humans","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b472","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b471","text":"This is where the value of the human creative lies. Agents cannot feel the vibe of a cultural moment or understand the nuance of irony and empathy.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b475","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b473","text":"Setting the creative vision. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b474","text":"Deciding that a brand needs to feel nostalgic but futuristic rather than just modern.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b478","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b476","text":"Defining constraints. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b477","text":"Setting the ethical boundaries and the never-go zones for the AI.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b481","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b479","text":"Final quality gatekeeping. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b480","text":"The no or the yes. Looking at the 10 concepts generated by the agents and identifying the one that has the spark necessary for a successful campaign.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b483","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b482","text":"Orchestrating with Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"orchestrating-with-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b485","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b484","text":"Melius serves as the bridge between your strategic intent and the actual production of assets. It is the orchestration layer that prevents your workflow from devolving into a dozen browser tabs and disconnected conversations. When you use Melius, you aren't just sending a prompt to an AI; you are deploying a system-wide context.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b488","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b486","text":"Brand context, stored once. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b487","text":"You give Melius your brand context, written instructions plus reference images, and Mel applies it to every prompt, node title, and output automatically, so the work starts on-brand instead of you restating the rules each time.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b494","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b491","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b489","text":"The right model for each job. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b490","text":"A campaign spans copy, images, video, and audio, and no single model is best at all of them. Mel plans the work and routes each job to the best model across ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b492","text":"every major provider under one subscription","marks":["b491"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b493","text":", then lays the results out together on one canvas.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b497","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b495","text":"One shared context. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b496","text":"Because every generation draws on the same brief and the same brand context on one canvas, the pieces stay coherent. If the brief calls for a dark, cinematic tone, the copy Mel writes and the images it generates pull from that same intent instead of drifting apart across separate chats.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b500","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b498","text":"Steer in plain language. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b499","text":"Instead of rewriting prompts one at a time, you tell Mel what to change (make it more aggressive, warmer grade, tighter crop) and it reworks the affected pieces on the canvas for you.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b502","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b501","text":"This level of orchestration is what allows a single creative director to manage the output of what would traditionally be a 10-person production team.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b504","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b503","text":"Future-proofing the agency workflow","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"future-proofing-the-agency-workflow"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b506","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b505","text":"The competitive advantage in the next five years will not belong to the agency that uses AI; it will belong to the agency that masters the Brief-to-Execution workflow. The benefits are measurable.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b509","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b507","text":"Speed. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b508","text":"Moving from brief to a full-funnel campaign in hours instead of weeks.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b512","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b510","text":"Consistency. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b511","text":"Holding one brand context across thousands of assets, so the same intent shows up whether it's the first render or the ten-thousandth.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b515","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b513","text":"Scale. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b514","text":"Handling 5x the client volume without a 5x increase in headcount or overhead.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b517","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b516","text":"We are moving away from the magic-box view of AI, where you type a prompt and hope for a miracle. We are entering the era of the agentic workforce, where tools like Melius let you stop being an operator and start being a director. Your value is no longer in your ability to use the tools; it's in your ability to lead the system.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b522","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b519","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b518","text":"Move beyond the prompt. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b520","text":"Start directing your workflow with Melius","marks":["b519"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b521","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b524","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b523","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b525","items":"$44:props:post:faq"}]}}]
45:["$","$L43","post-seedance-2-5-anticipation",{"post":{"_key":"post-seedance-2-5-anticipation","slug":"seedance-2-5-anticipation","category":"modus-news","title":"Seedance 2.5 is coming: ByteDance's next-gen AI video model","isoDate":"2026-07-07","date":"July 7, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Seedance is behind more than a quarter of every video generation on Melius, and its share keeps climbing. ByteDance's Seedance 2.5 is announced with 50 reference inputs, synced audio, and, per its makers, native 4K. Here is the real usage data behind Seedance today, and an honest read on what 2.5 does and does not confirm.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/seedance-2-5/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is Seedance 2.5?","answer":"Seedance 2.5 is ByteDance's next-generation AI video model, announced on June 23, 2026. Per ByteDance, it generates clips up to 30 seconds long, accepts up to 50 multimodal reference inputs, and co-processes audio in the same latent space as the video so sound and action stay in sync. It has not been publicly released, so these are announced specifications rather than independently tested numbers."},{"question":"When is Seedance 2.5 coming out?","answer":"It is in global enterprise beta now, with public access rolling out in early July 2026. We route across every major model at Melius, so we will add Seedance 2.5 as soon as public access opens."},{"question":"What is new in Seedance 2.5 compared to Seedance 2.0?","answer":"The clearest change is reference capacity, up from 12 inputs to 50, covering images, audio, 3D white models, and style references. ByteDance also describes native audio synchronisation, local region editing, longer clips, and around 20% better prompt adherence. Native 4K with 10-bit color is reported too, though the 4K upgrade shown at the same event was attributed mainly to a Seedance 2.0 tier, and ByteDance has not published a separate resolution spec for 2.5, so treat 4K as an announced feature rather than a confirmed one."},{"question":"How much is Seedance used on Melius?","answer":"A lot. Seedance makes up 26.7% of all video generations on Melius, one of the two most-used video models on the platform, and about 4,400 teams have run it. Its share has climbed from 6.5% in March 2026 to nearly 30% today."},{"question":"How do you use Seedance 2.0?","answer":"You can use Seedance 2.0 on Melius today. Pick Seedance in the video model picker, give it a text prompt or, for production work, a reference image to animate, and run it. Because every model shares one credit pool, you can compare the same shot across Seedance, Kling and Veo side by side without juggling separate budgets."},{"question":"Is Seedance free to use?","answer":"Seedance runs on paid generation credits like every frontier video model. On Melius those credits are shared across every image, video and audio model in one pool, so you are not buying a separate Seedance subscription to try it."},{"question":"Will Seedance 2.5 be available on Melius?","answer":"It already is. Seedance 2.5 shipped and is in the Melius video model picker alongside Kling, Veo, Sora, and Wan, with 30-second clips, generated audio, and up to 50 reference files."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"see-it-for-yourself","title":"See It"},{"_key":"a-quarter-of-every-video-and-climbing","title":"The Numbers"},{"_key":"what-ai-video-generation-models-struggle-at","title":"The Hard Part"},{"_key":"get-ready-for-it","title":"Get Ready"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b157","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b154","text":"Right now, over a quarter of video generation traffic on Melius is routed to Seedance 2.0. Initially, Seedance wasn't heavily used, and didn't even cover a tenth of our generations in regards to videos. It just quietly became one of the models people here reach for when they need a quality video to post, and its share has climbed nearly every month since our inception in spring. When ByteDance announced ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b155","text":"Seedance 2.5","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b156","text":", it was not one more model to go and evaluate. It's an upgrade to something a lot of users are already excited about and are still pushing the boundaries of.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b159","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b158","text":"This piece is two things: what our own generation data says about how people use Seedance right now, and a read on what 2.5 promises. The usage numbers here are ours, and they are pulled directly from our data. Seedance 2.5 is not public yet, so its specs are based on what info ByteDance has released on it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b161","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b160","text":"See it for yourself","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"see-it-for-yourself"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b163","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b162","text":"Start with the output, because that is what earns the usage. These are real Seedance 2.0 generations from Melius, one model across four different jobs: a product beauty shot, a character moment, a cinematic frame, and a scene with a lot of motion. Not a cherry-picked hero reel, just the kind of work people run through it every day.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"videoCompare","_key":"b164","caption":"Real Seedance 2.0 output on Melius, the same model across four different jobs. ByteDance says 2.5 extends work like this to 30-second clips with synced audio and higher resolution.","clips":[{"label":"Product","src":"/videos/blog/seedance-2-5/seedance-product.mp4","poster":"/images/hero/hero-1.webp","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"},{"label":"Character","src":"/videos/blog/seedance-2-5/seedance-character.mp4","poster":"/images/hero/hero-2.webp","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"},{"label":"Cinematic","src":"/videos/blog/seedance-2-5/seedance-cinematic.mp4","poster":"/images/hero/hero-3.webp","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"},{"label":"Motion","src":"/videos/blog/seedance-2-5/seedance-motion.mp4","poster":"/images/hero/hero-4.webp","aspectRatio":"16 / 9"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b166","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b165","text":"A quarter of every video, and climbing","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-quarter-of-every-video-and-climbing"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b170","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b167","text":"Seedance is not something people just experiment with and forget on the platform. It is behind ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b168","text":"26.7% of every video generation on Melius","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b169","text":", one of only two models that carry the bulk of video work here, and around 4,400 teams have used it. Last week its share sat near 30%. What makes that striking is how fast it happened.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"lineChart","_key":"b171","title":"The rise of Seedance on Melius","caption":"Seedance's share of finished video jobs on Melius. From low usage in March to more than a quarter of all video work, Seedance has become one of the most-used video models on our platform.","unit":"%","yMax":30,"points":[{"label":"March","value":1},{"label":"April","value":10},{"label":"May","value":22},{"label":"June","value":30}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b173","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b172","text":"That entire climb ran on Seedance 2.0 alone. Nobody was pushed onto it or was even the model that we automatically routed to. People tried it against everything else we offer, side by side, and kept coming back. That is the useful signal, and it is why a generational update matters more here than a version number usually would.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b178","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b175","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b174","text":"There is a tell in how they use it. In our data, where we can see the mode, image-to-video beats text-to-video by more than a 2:1 ratio. This is the proof that Seedance is used for production quality videos, not just novelty prompting. People are not prompting Seedance with â€œcat astronautâ€ to see what happens. They are bringing a frame they already validated, a product, a character, a locked composition they love, and asking the model to move it and use it as a reference without breaking it. That starting frame is usually generated in an image model first, which is why picking the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b176","text":"right Nano Banana model","marks":["b175"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b177","text":" for the still feeds directly into a better clip.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b180","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b179","text":"What AI video generation models struggle at","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-ai-video-generation-models-struggle-at"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b182","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b181","text":"A clip that looks good for three seconds is a solved problem. Most modern models clear that bar. The hard part, the part that decides whether AI video is a toy or a tool, is everything after those three seconds: holding a face across a shot, keeping a product on-model, running long enough to be usable, carrying its own sound, and not forcing you to throw away a great take because one detail came out wrong.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b184","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b183","text":"Read the Seedance 2.5 feature list with that in mind and it stops looking like a spec dump. Every headline item is aimed at exactly those production problems. One caveat before the list: Seedance 2.5 is not public yet, so what follows is ByteDance's announcement, not a benchmark.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b187","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b185","text":"Up to 50 reference inputs, from 12. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b186","text":"Four times the old ceiling, spanning images, audio, 3D white models, and style guides. That is what it takes to hold a character or a brand steady across a longer shot instead of watching it drift frame by frame.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b190","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b188","text":"Native audio, in one pass. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b189","text":"Audio and video are generated together, in the same latent space, so sound is matched to the action rather than dubbed on afterward. This is the feature people already fake today with a separate audio step.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b193","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b191","text":"Local editing. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b192","text":"Fix one region of a clip without regenerating the whole thing, so a single wrong detail no longer costs you the take you liked. At 30 seconds a clip, that is the difference between an edit and a reroll.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b196","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b194","text":"Longer clips. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b195","text":"Up to 30 seconds in a single generation, with a beta mode reaching three minutes. Long enough to be a finished shot, not a loop.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b197","rows":[{"_key":"b198","cells":[{"_key":"b199","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b201","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b200","text":"Capability","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b202","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b204","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b203","text":"Seedance 2.5 (as announced)","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b205","cells":[{"_key":"b206","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b208","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b207","text":"Reference inputs","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b209","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b211","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b210","text":"Up to 50 multimodal inputs, up from 12","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b212","cells":[{"_key":"b213","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b215","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b214","text":"Audio","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b216","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b218","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b217","text":"Co-processed with video for native sound sync","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b219","cells":[{"_key":"b220","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b222","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b221","text":"Editing","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b223","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b225","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b224","text":"Local region edits without a full regeneration","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b226","cells":[{"_key":"b227","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b229","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b228","text":"Clip length","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b230","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b232","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b231","text":"Up to 30 seconds, with a beta mode reaching 3 minutes","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b233","cells":[{"_key":"b234","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b236","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b235","text":"Resolution","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b237","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b239","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b238","text":"4K capabilities, 10-bit color (claimed, disputed)","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b240","cells":[{"_key":"b241","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b243","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b242","text":"Prompt adherence","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b244","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b246","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b245","text":"Around 20% better, per ByteDance","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b247","cells":[{"_key":"b248","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b250","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b249","text":"Availability","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b251","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b253","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b252","text":"Enterprise beta now, public access in early July 2026","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b255","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b254","text":"The references jump and the audio change are the two most consistently reported, and the two that map most directly onto how people already work. ByteDance also reports 4K capabilities with 10-bit color and roughly 20% better prompt adherence, though the 4K figure is muddier than the rest, since the same event also gave Seedance 2.0 its own native 4K tier. It was announced June 23, 2026, and is to release soon.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b257","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b256","text":"Get ready for it","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"get-ready-for-it"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b259","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b258","text":"Seedance 2.5 joins the Melius video picker the moment public access opens. Three things set you up before it does.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b262","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b260","text":"Keep building with Seedance 2.0. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b261","text":"It is one of the strongest video models on the platform today, and everything you learn about prompting it carries straight over.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b265","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b263","text":"Gather your references. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b264","text":"If you have been rationing reference frames to fit the old limit, start collecting the full set now. 2.5 gives you room for up to 50.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b271","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b268","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b266","text":"Compare it against the field. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b267","text":"Run the same shot through Seedance, Kling, and Veo side by side. Because Melius puts ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b269","text":"every model under one subscription","marks":["b268"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b270","text":" and one credit pool, you can mass produce and compare videos without juggling separate budgets, so you get the best chance of landing the video you want.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b273","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b272","text":"If 2.5 delivers even most of what is on the sheet, it sharpens every reason people picked it in the first place.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b279","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b276","href":"/blog/seedance-2-5","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b274","text":"Update: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b275","text":"Seedance 2.5 has since shipped. See ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b277","text":"what Seedance 2.5 actually supports on Melius","marks":["b276"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b278","text":" for the released specs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b284","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b281","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b280","text":"Want to see how your own generations break down by model? ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b282","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b281"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b283","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b286","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b285","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b287","items":"$45:props:post:faq"}]}}]
